/// Lesson sections for the info page — never shown on the practice screen.
const List<TechniqueSection> setFillSextupletsLesson = [
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Why it matters",
    body:
        "Sextuplets down the toms are the fast, rolling fill of rock and fusion. The pad sheet \"Sextuplet Fill\" gave you six even notes per beat; on the kit they have to change drums on the beat and still meet the kick and the crash on time.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "How to play it",
    body:
        "Three bars of rock eighths, crash on the one of bar 1. In line 1 two beats of sextuplets sit on the snare, beat 3 on the high tom, beat 4 on the floor tom. The kick plays 1 and 3 together with the first note of each six. Change drums with the right hand on the first note of the beat.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Practice tips",
    body:
        "Line 2 accents each six and walks snare, high tom, mid tom, floor tom. Line 4 swaps sixteenths and sextuplets on the high tom, then again on the floor tom: the gear change happens on one drum. Line 5 is R L R R L L on the snare for three beats and on the floor tom for beat 4, line 7 R L L R L L over all four toms. Start slow enough that six really are six. Toms accept any tom and the crash any crash, so a kit with fewer drums plays the sheet too: the mid tom and the second floor tom go to the nearest tom you have.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Where you hear it",
    body:
        "Rock and fusion tom runs at the end of a chorus, Mike Portnoy, Vinnie Colaiuta.",
  ),
];
